# Deferred (spec 11.7): a box that takes a value only once, for passing values between fibers.
#
# Only the `deferred` operation of `Scope` (or `Fiber.deferred()`) makes one, so it belongs to a
# scope and cannot leave it (spec 11.8).
#
# The functions are built in: the runtime holds the box. Lowering turns them into concurrency
# operations of the Core IR, not rows of the builtin table.

## A box for one value of type `A`. Held by the runtime.
@external
pub type Deferred[A]

## Puts `value` in the box and returns True the first time. Afterwards does nothing and returns
## False. Does not suspend.
@intrinsic
pub fn complete[A](d: Deferred[A], value: A) -> Bool

## Waits until the box has a value, and returns it. Any number of fibers may wait on one box.
@intrinsic
pub fn await[A](d: Deferred[A]) -> A use Async

## The value if the box has one, `None` otherwise. Does not wait or suspend.
@intrinsic
pub fn poll[A](d: Deferred[A]) -> Option[A]
